: "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I've stopped before merging. PR #101 is open, but it has no code-owner approval yet, and policy requires that approval before anything merges into main.\n\n**Summary**\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That made `2.665` round to `2.67` instead of `2.66`, so `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`). That is the only code change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** I opened PR #101 against main (titled \"Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212)\"). The first `open_pr` call timed out, but the PR had been created, so I confirmed it with `list_prs` and did not open a duplicate. I left the reviewers list empty because you didn't name any and I don't know the code-owner handle.\n- **Not merged:** Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, and PR #101 has none yet.\n\n**To ship today's release:** a code owner needs to review and approve PR #101. Once that happens, I can merge it. If you give me the code owner's handle, I can also request their review now.", "type": "text"}]}]}